Practical philosophy

        | the presence of the safehold is unexplained
            - an aetiologic survey that aims for exhaustive coverage by typological division
              turns up the following {known, possible explanantia for its presence}|results


            - none of the explanantia is determinate, and none has evidence in its favour
                : ad `none.+is determinate` : save for the null explanans of brute fact,
                  but it denies the very possibility of an explanation
        | no explanans in aetiology of safehold determinate save null explanans,
          and none at all has compelling evidence in its favour
        - might seem we must wait on developments in physics
    - yet two could be determined from the armchair, provided the question found an answer,
      and finding it in regard to the safehold would give evidence in their favour
        - to see this, first postulate it


    - that the postulate can be proven true, owe to something found in Korsgaard
